WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
Brain stem cells limit dangerous blood pressure swings, even when average readings stay normal. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 228. After that, extra snap allotments and child maltreatment, a tomato enzyme that sets pest resistance, and imaging neural activity deeper in living brain. University of Virginia researchers found adrenergic neurons in the brain stem that keep blood pressure from swinging during sleep, waking, standing, and exercise. Only a few hundred of those cells do that job.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.820
in findings published in circulation research and funded by the National Institutes of Health.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.920
When the cells were lost, the readings jumped around from moment to moment.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.200
The same population is damaged or missing in multiple system atrophy,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.060
a rare fatal neurological disorder related to Parkinson's disease.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.920
Severe blood pressure dysregulation is a feature of that disorder.

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:56.255
Ten states ended COVID era snap emergency allotments on staggered schedules

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:59.995
while other states kept paying them, which set up a natural experiment.

00:01:00.495 --> 00:01:07.735
Child welfare records from 1,153 United States counties between January 2021 and February

00:01:07.735 --> 00:01:11.255
2022 were examined, according to Fizz.org.

00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:15.375
Those files came from the National Child Abuse and Neglect Data System.

00:01:16.015 --> 00:01:20.955
Counties that lost the extra allotments showed more substantiated maltreatment overall and

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.195
more neglect and physical abuse in particular.

00:01:23.195 --> 00:01:29.075
The increase built slowly after the payments stopped, as households lived with ongoing money pressure.

00:01:29.675 --> 00:01:37.575
Calls and reports into child welfare agencies did not rise in a significant way, so the shift tracked real cases rather than extra detection.

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:47.175
The American Journal of Preventative Medicine published the study, which concludes that nutrition assistance may support child and family well-being beyond food security alone.

00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:52.532
Households that suddenly lost several hundred dollars a month in food support faced strain

00:01:52.532 --> 00:01:53.952
that piled up over time.

00:01:54.512 --> 00:01:58.592
Neglect and physical abuse ran higher months later as that pressure accumulated.

00:01:59.172 --> 00:02:04.012
Because the cutoff rolled out in stages, the policy change could be separated from wider

00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:05.032
pandemic effects.

00:02:05.672 --> 00:02:09.192
Nutrition aid here operates as an upstream child protection measure.

00:02:09.692 --> 00:02:13.852
Taking it away brings measurable costs for families already stretched by hardship.

00:02:13.852 --> 00:02:20.139
chip. Wild tomatoes fend off the pest thorumea absoluta, more effectively than cultivated lines,

