00:04:12.512 --> 00:04:17.952
Teams at TU Ween and the University of California San Diego fired intense ultraviolet pulses

00:04:17.952 --> 00:04:18.932
at helium atoms.

00:04:19.632 --> 00:04:23.792
Both of helium's electrons came free and then returned to the nucleus together through

00:04:23.792 --> 00:04:24.792
quantum correlation.

00:04:25.492 --> 00:04:30.052
The energy they carried together produced x-ray photons past the usual single electron

00:04:30.052 --> 00:04:30.672
