00:05:44.375 --> 00:05:50.235
A University of York and WWF report gathered place-based visions from towns and cities across the

00:05:50.235 --> 00:05:50.935
United Kingdom.

00:05:50.935 --> 00:05:56.515
them. People there described practical adaptations that keep livelihoods intact, cut emissions,

00:05:56.855 --> 00:06:01.675
and raise resilience to heat, flooding, and other shifting conditions. Local knowledge

00:06:01.675 --> 00:06:07.134
in the report is positioned to inform national and international climate strategies. Most

00:06:07.134 --> 00:06:11.474
people assume a meteor simply burns up or evaporates in a bright streak of heat and light.

00:06:12.034 --> 00:06:17.654
What the rock is actually doing, in video and photographs of 75 documented falls, is melting

00:06:17.654 --> 00:06:23.074
and breaking apart. Straight forward evaporation is not what decides how much mass makes it to the

00:06:23.074 --> 00:06:28.754
ground. A shockwave forms as the body first hits the upper atmosphere, and the surface starts to

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:34.394
glow. Mass loss then shifts to melting, and the airflow strips molten droplets off the rock.

00:06:35.034 --> 00:06:40.354
Up to 40% of the original mass can leave that way once the fireball steadies around 60 kilometers

00:06:40.354 --> 00:06:45.834
altitude. Pieces start to break away at air pressures only about one-fifth the compressive strength

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:51.134
measured later in recovered meteorites. Heating on the way in, plus collisions the rock already

00:06:51.134 --> 00:06:56.314
took in space, leave weaknesses so fragments come off well before peak dynamic stress.

00:06:57.014 --> 00:07:01.374
An intact rear-phase holds together long enough to throw a low-pressure wake behind it.

00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:06.414
Smaller shards get funneled in that wake and reach the ground in narrow strips instead of a wide

00:07:06.414 --> 00:07:12.544
scatter. Meteoridics and planetary science carried the seven-stage sequence after that video and

00:07:12.544 --> 00:07:19.044
photo-analysis. In phase four, melting settles into a stable balance. In phase five, fragmentation

00:07:19.044 --> 00:07:24.923
speeds up both mass loss and deceleration. The full sequence accounts for rocks that still

00:07:24.923 --> 00:07:30.203
reach the surface and for others that explode or vanish high up. Airbursts and strewn field

00:07:30.203 --> 00:07:35.103
models need fragmentation thresholds and wake dynamics in them, rather than leaning mainly

00:07:35.103 --> 00:07:41.239
on ablation rates. Mushrooms hold specific fungal molecules being checked for effects on cellular

00:07:41.239 --> 00:07:47.959
or aging pathways. A review on bioengineer.org ways whether those compounds touch known longevity-related

00:07:47.959 --> 00:07:53.299
processes. The evidence is still preliminary and comes from laboratory models rather than human

00:07:53.299 --> 00:07:59.790
trials. Briefly, a gene therapy approach described by the Hindu is being tested to silence integrated

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:06.890
hepatitis B viral DNA rather than going after active replication alone. A new tissue atlas maps how

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:11.970
cells sit and how neighbors interact across tumor samples to train machine learning models

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.470
that predict disease behavior.

